str_to_date [SimTalk]
Converts the specified date-statement into a statement of data type date.
Remarks
Conversion depends on the setting you selected under File > Model Settings/Preferences > Units > Time
Scale.
Type
Function
Syntax
str_to_date(DateStatement:string) → date
Parameter
The parameter DateStatement of data type string designates the date that you want to convert. The year
either has two or four digits. The function also takes leap years into account.
You can specify the date in these formats: "YYYY/MM/DD", "YYYY-MM-DD", and "DD.MM.YYYY".
Return Value
The return value has the data type date.
Example
print str_to_date("2024/02/10") // 2024/02/10
print str_to_date("2024-02-10") // 2024/02/10
print str_to_date("10.02.2024") // 2024/02/10
See also
isValidDateString [SimTalk]
Time Scale [preferences]
str_to_date [SimTalk]
